ification","dayOfWeek":["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday"],"opens":"08:00","closes":"18:00"}],"priceRange":"$$"},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/#website","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/","name":"Oregon Insurance Appraiser","publisher":{"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/#webpage","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/","name":"How Insurance Appraisal Works in Oregon | 8 Stages","description":"How insurance appraisal works in Oregon, in eight stages: the written demand, naming appraisers, the umpire, negotiation and the binding award.","inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/#website"},"about":{"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"dateModified":"2026-11-16","primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/#primaryimage","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/plans-clipboard.webp","width":960,"height":640},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/#breadcrumb"},"mainEntity":{"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/#howto"}},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"The appraisal path","item":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/"}],"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/#breadcrumb"},{"@type":"HowTo","name":"How insurance appraisal works in Oregon","description":"The eight stages of a property insurance appraisal, from disagreement to signed award.","step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"A disagreement on the number","text":"The insurer accepts the claim but its estimate is lower than yours. You have asked for a re-inspection or sent a supplement, and the gap remains.","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"The written demand","text":"Either side sends a written demand for appraisal that identifies the claim, the disagreement and the clause being invoked.","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"Each side names an appraiser","text":"Within the time the policy sets, often 20 days, each side names a competent, disinterested appraiser and tells the other.","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"The appraisers pick an umpire","text":"The two appraisers agree on a neutral umpire. If they can’t, the policy usually lets either side ask a court to appoint one.","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":5,"name":"Inspection and estimates","text":"Your appraiser inspects, measures and writes an independent, line-item estimate. The other appraiser does the same.","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":6,"name":"Working the differences","text":"The appraisers compare estimates item by item and agree what they can. Most of the gap usually closes here.","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":7,"name":"Umpire review","text":"Items still open go to the umpire, who reviews both appraisers’ support and decides each one.","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":8,"name":"The signed award","text":"An award signed by any two of the three sets the amount of loss. The insurer then pays under the policy’s terms.","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/"}],"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/oregon-appraisal-roadmap/#howto"}]}</script>
